# Keep the build context small and correct. Without this, `COPY . .` in the
# Dockerfile drags the host node_modules (built for the host OS/arch, not the
# Alpine builder) over the `npm ci` result and copies the stale local build —
# a cross-arch/staleness hazard and a >750 MB context.
#
# NOTE: .env is deliberately NOT ignored. It is a committed, secret-free template
# (secrets are injected server-side at runtime), and Next.js reads it at build to
# inline NEXT_PUBLIC_* flags into the standalone bundle. Local-only overrides
# (.env.local) are excluded below.

node_modules/
.next/
.git/
.gitignore

# Local, git-ignored env overrides (may hold developer-specific values).
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Logs and misc
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
